@startuml option-c-staging
title Staged roadmap and the DSL decision point

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor<<done>> #DDF2DD
  BackgroundColor<<dsl>> #FFE9C6
}

|Framework|
start
:Stage 0 (this branch)
reference_token, association<L,R,D>,
resolve<>() registration, pre-dispatch
resolution, post-dispatch local binding,
same-cell and ancestor-cell targets;<<done>>

:Stage 1
FORM round-trip of association<L,R,D>
(one generic container layout:
 cell_coordinate, product_locator, element, D);
note right
  No user dictionary needed: association
  is a framework type.  D must already be
  a persistable type.
end note

:Stage 2
Descendant / sibling cell targets
(gather operator: one message per
 target cell, keyed by cell_coordinate);

:Stage 3
Reference sets and many-to-many
convenience views (grouped iteration,
one-to-one enforcement at registration);

|Data-model DSL|
if (References embedded in user product
types (Hit contains ref<Wire>)?) then (yes)
  :**DSL decision point**
  YAML (or Jsonnet) product description with:
  - ref members: target concept, cardinality,
    cell scope (same | ancestor:<layer> | any)
  - schema_version + migration block
  Generator emits: C++ struct, resolved view
  struct, ROOT selection XML/LinkDef, HDF5
  compound layout, FORM descriptors;<<dsl>>
  :Stage 4
  Embedded references pre-resolved into
  generated "<T>_resolved" views;<<dsl>>
else (no)
  :Associations remain the only
  reference carrier; DSL optional;
endif

|Framework|
:Stage 5
Cross-file / cross-job references:
product_locator gains provenance
(process/stage chain) and FORM maps
locator -> file/container;
stop

@enduml
